---
/**
 * Printable recovery card (DR11): one small page a person prints and keeps
 * with their emergency papers. It tells them, or anyone helping them, how to
 * bring toolkit work back on any device. The wording is dictation-stable
 * (DR10): every name on this card can be read aloud over a phone.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Recovery card - Resilience Hub Toolkit"
  description="A printable card with the steps to bring your toolkit work back on any device."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10">
    <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground no-print">
      Print this and keep it with your emergency papers
    </p>

    <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border-2 border-border bg-card p-6 sm:p-8" id="recovery-card">
      <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">Resilience Toolkit recovery card</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-foreground">
        Your toolkit work lives on your own device, not in the cloud. A backup is a file you keep.
        This card tells you, or anyone helping you, how to bring that work back.
      </p>

      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-foreground list-decimal list-inside">
        <li>
          On the device you want the work on, open
          <strong>resiliencetoolkit.org/dashboard</strong>
        </li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Restore from a backup</strong></li>
        <li>
          Pick your backup file. Its name starts with
          <strong>resilience-toolkit-backup</strong>, then the date it was made
        </li>
        <li>The preview shows what the file holds before anything changes</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-foreground">
        Saying it over the phone: the site is resiliencetoolkit dot org, slash dashboard. The file
        is resilience dash toolkit dash backup, then the date.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
        Keep your backup file on a device you own, or print your key pages too. A fresh backup is
        one tap on the dashboard: Back up my work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <button
      id="print-card"
      class="no-print mt-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
      style="min-height: 44px"
    >
      Print this card
    </button>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('print-card')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      window.print();
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @media print {
    #recovery-card {
      border-color: #000;
    }
  }
</style>
